# Competiscan report pipelines — cron schedule.
# Install with:  crontab pipelines/cron/crontab.example
# (or open `crontab -e` and paste the three job lines below in).
#
# Before enabling, on the VM:
#   1. chmod +x pipelines/cron/*.sh
#   2. Edit pipelines/cron/common.sh — set CONDA_PYTHON to the real path of
#      the "research" conda env's python on this VM.
#   3. Confirm the repo + its prerequisites are all present at
#      /opt/automations: .env (PPT_BUILDER_LOGIN/PASSWORD), python-server.pem
#      (SSH key for the MySQL tunnel — see ConnectToDB_VPN_utils.py), and AWS
#      credentials for Bedrock + SES (~/.aws/credentials or an instance role).
#   4. Confirm the VM can actually reach: the MySQL host over SSH,
#      csresearchhub.com (PPT builder), and AWS. The pipelines fail loudly and
#      exit non-zero when any of these are unreachable — they do not silently
#      skip — so a failed run will show up in the logs under
#      pipelines/output/logs/.
#   5. Check the VM's timezone (`timedatectl`) — the hours below assume it
#      matches your local time; adjust if the VM runs in UTC or another zone.
#
# Optional: uncomment MAILTO so cron emails you if a wrapper script itself
# fails to even start (needs a local MTA/sendmail configured on the VM —
# separate from the pipelines' own SES-based report-ready emails).
# MAILTO=hgquijano@competiscan.com

# Harborstone weekly deck — every Monday at 6:00 AM, reports the week that
# just ended (Mon->Mon window, computed by the pipeline itself).
0 6 * * 1 /opt/automations/pipelines/cron/run_harborstone.sh

# Monthly Banking Merger — 23:59, but only fires on the LAST day of the month
# (the `[ ... ] &&` guard checks that tomorrow rolls over to day 01). The
# pipeline always reports on "the current month" at the moment it runs, so
# firing right before month-end is what makes that mean the complete month.
59 23 28-31 * * [ "$(date -d tomorrow +\%d)" = "01" ] && /opt/automations/pipelines/cron/run_merger.sh

# SupplyHouse.com competitor ads — 5:00 AM on the 1st of each month, reporting
# on the prior (now-complete) calendar month.
0 5 1 * * /opt/automations/pipelines/cron/run_supplyhouse.sh
